Subject: [PATCH 126/148] [ae-patch] Wait out dnd-kit's click blocker after
 each drag in the sort modes suite

A drop leaves dnd-kit's capture-phase click listener on document for 50 ms
(it removes it with setTimeout), and the suite's afterEach waits only 20 ms.
"applies the move on top of an order saved on another device" opens a row
menu and clicks Move to bottom right after the previous test's drag; when
the click landed inside that window it never reached React, the move never
ran, and the test failed waiting for the PUT. The drag helper now waits
50 ms after the drop, a timer that fires after dnd-kit's own.
---
 web/src/shell/Sidebar.aeSortModes.test.tsx | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/web/src/shell/Sidebar.aeSortModes.test.tsx b/web/src/shell/Sidebar.aeSortModes.test.tsx
index 813e07e26b52790c556838d7e5daff741fcd48e8..a560d7eb9fa3bd409a0e96be76475ac0361e48a8 100644
--- a/web/src/shell/Sidebar.aeSortModes.test.tsx
+++ b/web/src/shell/Sidebar.aeSortModes.test.tsx
@@ -226,6 +226,14 @@ async function drag(sourceId: string, targetId: string) {
   await act(async () => {
     fireEvent.mouseUp(document, target);
   });
+  // A drop leaves dnd-kit's click blocker (a capture-phase listener on document)
+  // up for 50 ms; a click before it lifts, in this test or the next, never
+  // reaches React. This timer starts after dnd-kit's, so it fires after it.
+  await act(async () => {
+    await new Promise((resolve) => {
+      setTimeout(resolve, 50);
+    });
+  });
   return insertion;
 }
 
